<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Acer Jan-Mar pretax down.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Acer Jan-Mar pretax down.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-March 1997</p>
<p>			 (in million T$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Turnover			     14,250 vs 16,220</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			   737 vs  1,067</p>
<p>NOTE - Acer Inc is Taiwan's largest computer firm.</p>
<p>A company statement said on Tuesday its earnings per share for the first three months was T$0.47. The statement attributed the first quarter profit decline to losses in its subsidaries in Europe and the United States.</p>
<p>Acer has set its 1997 net profit forecast at T$4 billion on sales of T$77.7 billion.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
